{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/333998-inserting-a-changeling-into-a-mix-splat-game-st-help-suggestion-request","id":333998,"title":"Inserting a changeling into a mix splat game [ST help/suggestion request]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T02:40:34-08:00","id":333998,"title":"Inserting a changeling into a mix splat game [ST help/suggestion request]","content":"I'm going to be running a small god-machine chronicle game with a few players(3-4) each playing different splats. I know for sure a werewolf and a changeling. My request is a critique on how I plan to introduce the changeling character. First off the game will take place on a man made island (by G.M. design) and each player for reasons unique to them will be there. The thought I had for the changeling character (which she will have veto power on) is 'what if her keeper ordered her to leave the hedge - to go where it can not and investigate what is going on - that her true escape may occur when she realizes she can be free'.<br /> <br /> Now the secondary part is a little more sly. I am going to try and aid the deception of what the changeling is. This is because before my time in the group, a few players burned in a stigma of changelings. Of course I will not give the changeling a free pass as it is a chance for other members to see the character before putting the stigma on them and the reveal of truth will be important (ofc I will also try and work out the scars of old players out of game). But how would you suggest I aid or allow a changeling to appear as another breed? For simplicity I imagine mage or demon may be the easiest for the changeling to pass itself off as at first or for a short time. The other side of the coin is what weaknesses would you recommend for this - how can I make it fair and give the other players a chance to see through the ruse. <br /> <br /> I also love the idea of throwing a good curve ball to add to character development and another layer to the story's complexity.<br /> <hr /><br /> If it helps in any way the island's construction will have been funded by a god-machine cult with the machine trying to gain an isolated testing ground of sorts. A city will have been built and populated by adds for new work and promises of a better life. Werewolf(s) will be probably be drawn there to maintain the reshaped shadow (decades construction and such putting the island as a reflection). Fae attention drawn simply by curiosity. Demons' attention because obviously something big is being planned (those who notice). etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T03:02:41-08:00","id":334039,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you have an idea for the premise, which is good. You might want to consider making sure your character will have some reason to both stick with the party and engage the main conflict that develops, lay the groundwork now so that things don't go at cross purposes later.<br /> <br /> I'd really recommend against trying to conceal the changeling's nature out of character. I can't see that going well; if the other players have negative preconceptions of changeling players, the eventual reveal stands a good chance of being an unwelcome surprise and reinforcing those attitudes reflexively. You should really just be up front with your fellow players, talk to them about what bothered them about their past experiences with changeling players, and make sure you're all on the same page and that they're comfortable with the idea.<br /> <br /> None of that is inconsistent with concealing the changeling's nature in character, of course. You don't really need much in the way of special tricks for that; changelings are already some of the World of Darkness's most elusive creatures, well able to hit ground when they want to. It really depends on the build, of course, and you might want to share some more elements of your concept for more specific advice, but honestly the easiest trick that occurs to me is simply to pretend to be a very capable and lucky human, maybe with a few weird tricks. The World of Darkness is filled with anomalies and exception cases, after all, and you don't exactly get handed an introductory pamphlet on all the major splats when you undergo the First Change or the like. If you're subtle with your pledgecraft and you don't go around opening doors into the Hedge, a lot of the contracts are very low-key, such that a non-mage probably wouldn't even realize you'd done anything when you use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T09:11:24-08:00","id":334260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/333998-inserting-a-changeling-into-a-mix-splat-game-st-help-suggestion-request?p=334039#post334039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really recommend against trying to conceal the changeling's nature out of character. I can't see that going well; if the other players have negative preconceptions of changeling players, the eventual reveal stands a good chance of being an unwelcome surprise and reinforcing those attitudes reflexively. You should really just be up front with your fellow players, talk to them about what bothered them about their past experiences with changeling players, and make sure you're all on the same page and that they're comfortable with the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stupid Loserman is neither stupid nor a loser.* I agree on all points, but especially this one. Concealing the Changeling from your players OOC is unlikely to improve the situation. If you have some idea about why your players feel the way they do, and are willing to share, forumites may be able to help you come up with ideas for counter-arguments when you talk to them about it, or ways of presenting the idea to your players.<br /> <br /> * May well be a man, but pattern recognition suggests I maybe shouldn't assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:33:51-08:00","id":334427,"title":"","content":"Thank you both, I've been iffy on the concealment anyway. I will be talking with them (originally planned to do so to prep for reveal down the road). What I do remember about what they complained about before was more the players' fault than anything inherent about changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}